import Tools.ShippingLeafDesign
import Tools.ShippingCombKidText

/-! # A SLOTLESS leaf machine as an entry, at the design level: the bridge, and what is still asked (round par/b-32)

WRITTEN, NOT BUILT.

`#machine_leaf_design` refuses a machine-route declaration without a
register ("slotless"). This file is what CAN be said for it from the built
theorems, and it states exactly what cannot.

## The route of a slotless leaf

A machine without calls and without slots compiles to an ASSIGNMENT-ONLY
module. Its ship-level endpoint is `f.machine_ships_comb`
(`Tools.ShippingMachineShipsComb.machine_ships_comb`, generated by
`#machine_endpoint`): under `∃ raw`, for every width map `wof`,

    simpleBody b = true →
    seqCheck wof (weOf wof) (checkedOptimize b).body = true →
    (seqNames (checkedOptimize b).body).all (declWidth … == weOf wof …) = true →
    MachineShipsComb f d (dropZeroWidthModule raw) (checkedOptimize b) wof dom src

`MachineShipsComb` is `MachineShips` without registers: no register list, no
start-register conditions, and the seeding `seedR` (the inputs, the name
`rst` low — a combinational module has no reset port).

## What is proved here

* `comb_design_of_ships` — PURE: `MachineShipsComb` at the emitter's own
  width map is, for the same environments, a closed run `DesignSV C 0 o`
  over every child map and every children's state, showing the source, and
  the only closed run (the analogue of
  `Tools.ShippingLeafDesign.leaf_design_of_ships`; the same two built
  lemmas `designSV0_of_leaf`, `designSV0_leaf_unique`).
* `comb_entry_outputs` — the full entry's module has the layout's output
  names (from the wired trace, as `machine_ships_comb` reads it; no world
  premise).
* `comb_entry_text_out` — conjuncts 2 and 3 of the text check of the full
  entry's module `b` ITSELF, for a leaf whose one output is `out`, from the
  run and `ChildBnd`: `leaf_run_typedIn_bnd` (which does not ask a slot) and
  `Tools.ShippingCombKidText.mergeChecked_text_out` (the validated merge of
  a typed module with the one output `out` stays typed).
* `comb_entry_design0_out` — the design-level statement in the shape of
  `f.machine_design_leaf0`, with TWO antecedents beside `ChildBnd`:

      ∃ raw, (b = dropZeroWidthModule raw ∨ b = mergeChecked (dropZeroWidthModule raw)) ∧
        (ChildBnd mref cref w →
         simpleBody b = true →                                         -- (S1) NOT ALLOWED
         (checkedOptimize b = b ∨ printOk (checkedOptimize b) = true) → -- (S2) NOT ALLOWED
         ∃ ids …, ∃ cache, ∀ i bools bits T ins st0 mems kids, (use conditions) →
           (∃ envsO, DesignSV (childMap design.modules) 0 (checkedOptimize b) (seedR b ins) T
               ⟨st0, mems, kids⟩ envsO ∧ envsO.length = T ∧ (the source on the outputs))
           ∧ ∀ envs', DesignSV … envs' → envs'.length = T ∧ (the source on the outputs))

  Against `f.machine_ships_comb`: the conclusion is `DesignSV` (with "every
  closed run shows the source"); of its three check antecedents the two
  about the EMITTED TEXT (`seqCheck`, the width agreement, at every `wof`)
  are gone; `simpleBody b = true` stays, and (S2) is new and smaller: a
  disjunction the compiler's register branch has as a theorem
  (`Tools.ShippingGuardsLeaf.checkedOptimize_instFree_print`) and its simple
  branch does not.

## What is NOT proved, exactly

(S1) `simpleBody b = true` for the full entry's module of a slotless
     machine. No theorem gives the right-hand-side SHAPES of a closed
     machine's assignments (`TypedIn` gives their widths). Where `b` is not
     of the simple shape the optimizer takes its `refineCheck` branch, for
     which there is no slotless ship-level theorem at all
     (`machine_ships_wired` asks a slot: it uses the reset input).
(S2) the text of the SHIPPED module on the simple branch.
     `checkedOptimize` keeps the optimizer's output there under `optCheck`,
     whose print conjunct binds only when `PrintCheck.moduleCheck b` holds
     (the uniform-width gate fragment) — there is no `printOk` guard as on
     the register branch. With (S1), (S2) would follow from the BUILT
     `Tools.ShippingControlOptSoundness.checkedOptimize_cast` /
     `checkedOptimize_control` (`checkedOptimize b = b` when the body has a
     slice, a concatenation, a NOT or a comparison) IF the body were known to
     contain such an assignment — `closeMachine` drives each output by a
     slice of the packed wire, but that again is a fact about shapes.
(S3) several outputs, or one output not named `out`: the text of the merged
     module (`docs/parallel/A-comb-kids.md` §2.3; the general statement about
     `TypedIn` is false). `comb_entry_text_out` asks the one output `out`.

(S1) and (S2) are properties of the run's module `b`, decidable on a
concrete module: `Tools/ShippingCombLeafCommand.lean` MEASURES them on the
real module of each declaration.

SCOPE of `comb_entry_design0_out`: one declaration as an entry, depth 0, no
call, no register, one output `out`; data conditions decided per declaration
(`CombKid`); the run, the reflection and `ChildBnd` stay premises, and (S1),
(S2) are OPEN obligations; `DesignSV` of the module list over the returned
design's child map — not the SV string, not `#sim`. The seeding is `seedR`
(`rst` low), not the register leaves' `seedIn`. -/
